3.1.2 Linear Discriminant Analysis
LDA is a supervised feature extraction method that has been extensively studied in the fields of statistics and pattern recognition. It aims to find the optimal transformation of features by training samples and their corresponding class labels. This allows for the extraction of discriminant features that can represent multiple types of objects [49]. The main idea of LDA is to maximize
the distance between data belonging to different classes and minimize the distance within groups after projection. LDA is closely related to regression analysis, such as linear regression [50] and logistic regression, making it suitable for solving regression and classification problems. For gas response signals from multi-sensor arrays, LDA can be used not only for data preprocessing but also for the classification of different gases.
