ion degree, and protein denaturation degree, respectively. Hence, these three indicators demonstrate that the utilization of gas sensors combined with machine learning algorithms can effectively evaluate and predict the freshness of frozen fish. Grassi et al. [143] designed a convenient and cheap E-nose system consisting of four MOS sensors to achieve the freshness of different seafood species only through a single classification model. Figure 8c is a PCA double image of the electronic nose data of the three fish species. The color difference represents the different freshness levels determined by the K-means. It can be seen that the classification of
